         <change when="2025-12-11T07:33:54-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - One correction: lin16-17 ἄσπα|[σαι] =&gt; ἀσπά|ζ̣ο̣[υ], where despite the ink blotches the contours of the zeta and omicron are visible. In lin16 Turner's proposal to change ῥ[ώ]σω =&gt; ῥ[αί]σω is confirmed by the current image, where one can actually see both alpha and iota. I've added dots and a trema as the verb is trisyllabic.</change>
